{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg-1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Since 7 and 11 are both prime, a number divisible by both must be a multiple of their product:\n\n**lcm(7, 11) = 7 × 11 = 77**\n\nSo the candidates are 77, 154, 231, and so on. The smallest is 77. It also has to be odd so that 2 doesn't divide it:\n\n- 77 ÷ 7 = 11 ✓\n- 77 ÷ 11 = 7 ✓\n- 77 ÷ 2 = 38.5, so 2 does not divide it ✓\n\nNo smaller positive number works, because every common multiple of 7 and 11 is a multiple of 77.\n\n**Answer: 77**"}]}}
